{
 "about": "The encyclopedias of each language's pack: Kiwix's ZIM files (download.kiwix.org, by name; each checked against the SHA-256 Kiwix publishes beside it), each put in a zip of its own (LastbookData/library-data/collections/<file>) in the data release, with a note of what it holds (encyclopedia-<file>.json). A language's pack is the starter pack's zip with that language's encyclopedias (packaging/data/encyclopedias.sh, run by the Encyclopedias workflow; its entry is made again whenever the starter pack changes). Wikipedia's and Wikivoyage's articles are their authors', under CC BY-SA 4.0, as Kiwix packs them. A release file is at most 2 GiB: English has the opening of Wikipedia's most read articles (mini) instead of their whole text (2.6 GB); Polish has no medical selection on Kiwix.",
